                <pb facs="0740" n="678" xml:id="pg678"/>

                <p rendition="#center">(Sent from Reynosa April 29, 1878. Received at the city of
                    Mexico at 10.13 p.m.)</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Citizen Minister of War:</p>
                <p>A party of revolutionists from Texas, numbering 100, were to-day beaten and
                    dispersed at Capote’s ranch. They left several prisoners, nine Spencer rifles,
                    and a horse in the hands of the government forces.</p>
                <closer><signed>R. CUELLAR.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
